To run local cluster we do not need to specify the master cluster in teh code we can use spark-submit code

spark-submit as this:

URL="spark://Amits-MacBook-Air.local:7077"

spark-submit \
    --master="${URL}" \
    10_spark_local.py \
        --input_green="data/pq/green/2020/*/" \
        --input_yellow="data/pq/yellow/2020/*/" \
        --output=data/report-2020

        stop the owrker and master after work


DataProc:
--input_green=gs://batch-processing-study/pq/green/2020/*/
--input_yellow=gs://batch-processing-study/pq/yellow/2020/*/
--output=gs://batch-processing-study/report-2020

location of script: gs://batch-processing-study/code/10_spark_local.py


Submit job using cloud SDK:

gcloud dataproc jobs submit pyspark \
    --cluster=de-zc-cluster \
    --region=us-central1 \
    gs://batch-processing-study/code/10_spark_local.py \
    -- \
        --input_green="gs://batch-processing-study/pq/green/2021/*/" \
        --input_yellow="gs://batch-processing-study/pq/yellow/2021/*/" \
        --output=gs://batch-processing-study/report-2021